{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836118",
      "title": "Tailwind CSS: Pros & Cons",
      "sourceHash": "f2e7a3db2267b1a4e41bd35ffcad84abd9af5993618a222426643ca4da4730a9",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.08,
          "end": 3.03,
          "en": "And that's it for this introduction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.03,
          "end": 5.76,
          "en": "to Tailwind CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.76,
          "end": 8.631,
          "en": "Now, as you can tell, when using Tailwind CSS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.631,
          "end": 11.607,
          "en": "you do end up with certain elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.607,
          "end": 14.915,
          "en": "that have a lot of CSS classes on them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.915,
          "end": 16.946,
          "en": "and that of course means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.946,
          "end": 20.883,
          "en": "that there is more code to add in your JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.883,
          "end": 23.887,
          "en": "And there certainly also are developers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.887,
          "end": 27.3,
          "en": "who don't like having long class name lists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.3,
          "end": 29.16,
          "en": "as we have it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.16,
          "end": 31.163,
          "en": "Though it's of course worth mentioning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.163,
          "end": 35.709,
          "en": "that Tailwind does actually work with React really well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.709,
          "end": 40.453,
          "en": "because you can create reusable utility Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.453,
          "end": 42.271,
          "en": "like this input Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.271,
          "end": 46.764,
          "en": "which then have all these CSS classes inside of them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.764,
          "end": 49.68,
          "en": "so that you can use them in your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.68,
          "end": 53.31,
          "en": "without having to repeat these long class lists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.31,
          "end": 55.173,
          "en": "over and over again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.7,
          "end": 58.47,
          "en": "Instead, as you can see here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.47,
          "end": 62.01,
          "en": "these custom input Components can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.01,
          "end": 65.822,
          "en": "in a pretty lean and easy to understand way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.822,
          "end": 69.99,
          "en": "and all these CSS classes are simply hidden",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.99,
          "end": 71.52,
          "en": "inside of the Component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.52,
          "end": 74.493,
          "en": "Therefore, we don't have to repeat this all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.23,
          "end": 78.53999999999999,
          "en": "So when embracing Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.53999999999999,
          "end": 81.55799999999999,
          "en": "as you should do when building React apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.55799999999999,
          "end": 83.714,
          "en": "embracing Tailwind CSS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.714,
          "end": 87.18,
          "en": "and this idea of building Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.18,
          "end": 89.15299999999999,
          "en": "by combining multiple classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.15299999999999,
          "end": 91.863,
          "en": "does actually work really well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.85,
          "end": 96.405,
          "en": "Nonetheless, using Tailwind CSS is, of course, something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.405,
          "end": 99.21000000000001,
          "en": "that like all these approaches in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.21000000000001,
          "end": 102,
          "en": "comes down to personal preference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102,
          "end": 104.97,
          "en": "An advantage of Tailwind CSS is that you don't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.97,
          "end": 107.731,
          "en": "really have to know CSS to use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.731,
          "end": 112.731,
          "en": "and you can develop React apps or web apps in general",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.95,
          "end": 117.408,
          "en": "to be precise pretty rapidly when using Tailwind CSS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.408,
          "end": 122.23,
          "en": "because as you'll see, it doesn't take you very long",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.23,
          "end": 125.977,
          "en": "to memorize the most important utility classes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.977,
          "end": 129.72,
          "en": "and especially with this nice extra extension,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.72,
          "end": 132.78,
          "en": "which even suggests classes and helps you find",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.78,
          "end": 135.87,
          "en": "the right classes, styling elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.87,
          "end": 140.19,
          "en": "and Components is actually pretty easy and done quickly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.19,
          "end": 142.173,
          "en": "when using Tailwind CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.083,
          "end": 146.52,
          "en": "You also avoid style clashes, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.52,
          "end": 151.143,
          "en": "because you don't define any global CSS rules on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.37,
          "end": 156.03,
          "en": "And Tailwind CSS gives you all these advantages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 156.03,
          "end": 160.38,
          "en": "whilst still being highly configurable and customizable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.38,
          "end": 163.2,
          "en": "and extensible so that you can really tweak it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.2,
          "end": 165.873,
          "en": "exactly to your likings and requirements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.772,
          "end": 170.132,
          "en": "But you do, of course, end up with those",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.132,
          "end": 174.21,
          "en": "relatively long class name values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.21,
          "end": 176.403,
          "en": "at least for certain elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 177.27,
          "end": 180.81,
          "en": "And any style changes that should be applied, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.81,
          "end": 183.799,
          "en": "do require the editing of JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.799,
          "end": 186.87,
          "en": "so you don't really have a strong separation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 186.87,
          "end": 190.47899999999998,
          "en": "between JSX and styling code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.47899999999998,
          "end": 193.23,
          "en": "And you also tend to end up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.23,
          "end": 196.6,
          "en": "with a lot of relatively small wrapper Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.6,
          "end": 200.13,
          "en": "like this input or button Component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.13,
          "end": 202.29,
          "en": "which isn't too bad though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.29,
          "end": 205.173,
          "en": "After all that's the idea behind React kind of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 206.46,
          "end": 208.74,
          "en": "Creating and using them can still sometimes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 208.74,
          "end": 210.63,
          "en": "be cumbersome and annoying.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.63,
          "end": 213.3,
          "en": "Or if you don't do that, you would end up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 213.3,
          "end": 215.71,
          "en": "with a lot of copy and pasting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 215.71,
          "end": 220.17000000000002,
          "en": "because if you don't create that input component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.17000000000002,
          "end": 223.89,
          "en": "you will have to copy and paste that code to all the inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.89,
          "end": 226.53300000000002,
          "en": "and labels you want to use in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 227.43,
          "end": 229.8,
          "en": "And therefore, as for all these solutions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 229.8,
          "end": 231.15,
          "en": "shown in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 231.15,
          "end": 233.88,
          "en": "there are various advantages and disadvantages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 233.88,
          "end": 237.03,
          "en": "but now since you got an introduction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 237.03,
          "end": 239.04,
          "en": "to all these different approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.04,
          "end": 242.28,
          "en": "for your future projects, you can hopefully pick",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 242.28,
          "end": 245.133,
          "en": "the solution you personally like most.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 246.06,
          "end": 249.98,
          "en": "For this course, I will mostly stick to Vanilla CSS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 249.98,
          "end": 254.637,
          "en": "simply because it allows me to focus on teaching you React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 254.637,
          "end": 258.565,
          "en": "and it avoids writing all those extra CSS class names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 258.565,
          "end": 260.185,
          "en": "But in your projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 260.185,
          "end": 264.783,
          "en": "you should definitely use the approach you personally like.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}